+# Homepage media
+
+These files are local so playback does not depend on third-party media hosts.
+
+- `hero.mp4`: silent, compressed 18-second excerpt from [Pexels video 3129977](https://www.pexels.com/video/3129977/). Original: https://videos.pexels.com/video-files/3129977/3129977-hd_1280_720_30fps.mp4
+- `roasting.mp4`: silent, compressed footage of roasted beans being processed, by [cottonbro studio on Pexels](https://www.pexels.com/video/processed-coffee-beans-ready-for-packing-4820350/). Original: https://videos.pexels.com/video-files/4820350/4820350-hd_720_1366_25fps.mp4
+- Both stock videos are available under the [Pexels License](https://www.pexels.com/license/). WebP posters are frames extracted from their respective clips.
+- `coffee-break.mp3`: original short podcast preview narrated with FFmpeg's Flite `slt` voice. Its complete spoken script appears in the homepage's transcript disclosure. It has no music or other sounds.
+
+The hero is eager. Below-the-fold players keep posters and media sources in inert `data-*` attributes and use `preload="none"` until within 200 pixels of the viewport. `media.js` then attaches URLs and enables metadata preloading. Native `loading="lazy"` is also included; the observer gate applies across browsers because native media lazy loading is not universally supported. No media autoplays.
+
+Without IntersectionObserver, user focus or pointer interaction activates the player. Without JavaScript, explicit links beneath each offscreen player open the media without initiating downloads on page load.
+
+Run the non-browser loading checks with `npm test`. No build step is required.
